      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremond%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1878, Francis Marion Wootan discovered mineral‑rich water in the area, which he bottled and marketed for its healing properties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremond%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wootan Wells grew into a resort community with four hotels and hundreds of staff before fires and droughts ended its boom in the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremond%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today Bremond is part of the Bryan‑College Station metropolitan area, linking it to one of Texas’s largest college towns.",
